# Harmonics Melody (repertoire plan: st-lick-harmonics). An original 8-bar bell tune in G major,
# played only with natural harmonics on strings 4, 3 and 2. Touch the string lightly right over
# the fret wire and pick:
#   over fret 12 the strings sound D, G and B (an octave above the open strings),
#   over fret 7 they sound A, D and F# (an octave and a fifth above),
#   over fret 5 they sound D, G and B again, two octaves above.
# Bars 1-4 rise at fret 12, turn at fret 7 and fall back down string 4 (frets 5, 7, 12) to D.
# Bars 5-8 start the same, echo the rising G chord an octave higher at fret 5, climb the D chord
# at fret 7 and land on a G chord rung at fret 5 (F# rising to G). The teacher strums G and D.
title: Harmonics Melody
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study for natural harmonics
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 4
tags: harmonics, natural harmonics, bell tone, let ring
tempo: 60
time: 4/4
key: G

track: Your harmonics
role: lead
